4. **Submission gate:**
   `POST /api/v1/upload/check` and `POST /api/v1/upload/agent` (`apps/platform/ditto/api_server/endpoints/upload.py`)
   - Refuse a hotkey that has no valid signature for the **currently effective** version.
   - Error tells miner to run `ditto cla sign`.
   - In `off`: check is skipped (or always passes).
   - In `shadow`: unsigned uploads are logged and counted (e.g., logger.warning or metrics/db count or shadow log), but upload is accepted.
   - In `enforce`: if unsigned (or signed outdated version), return error (e.g. HTTP 403 or 400 with detail: e.g. "Contributor License Agreement (CLA) signature required for hotkey. Please run `ditto cla sign` to sign CLA version {version}.").
   - `ditto upload` checks this up front before packaging or any payment step!

5. **`ditto cla sign` and `ditto cla status` in CLI:**
   - `ditto cla sign`:
     - fetches current CLA from Platform (`/api/v1/cla/current` or from `docs/legal/CLA-v<N>.md` / platform URL)
     - downloads text, recomputes SHA-256, verifies match
     - shows the CLA text (or summary/path + digest)
     - asks for explicit typed confirmation (e.g., prompt miner to type "I AGREE" or "yes" or "sign")
     - generates nonce (uuid4 or hex) and issued_at (current unix timestamp)
     - builds message: `f"ditto-cla:v1:{netuid}:{cla_version}:{cla_sha256}:{hotkey}:{nonce}:{issued_at}"`
     - signs with hotkey (sr25519)
     - sends payload to Platform `POST /api/v1/cla/sign`
     - prints success with signed version and signature
   - `ditto cla status`:
     - queries Platform `GET /api/v1/cla/status/{hotkey}`
     - shows signed version, whether it is current, signed_at time, signature digest/status.

